{"id": "whcalakmul", "name": "Calakmul Biosphere Reserve", "short": "Calakmul", "place": "Campeche, Mexico", "lat": 18.5, "lon": -89.8, "side": "l", "cont": "North America", "country": "Mexico", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Maya rainforest where jaguars, tapirs and fruit trees depend on scarce water.", "tip": {"id": "jaguar", "title": "Remove the jaguar", "text": "Lower Jaguar and watch the ripple: deer, peccaries, agoutis and monkeys lose a major predator, and vultures lose a source of carrion."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Calakmul Biosphere Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calakmul_Biosphere_Reserve"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Calakmul", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calakmul"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Baird's tapir", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baird%27s_tapir"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Jaguar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Geoffroy's spider monkey", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoffroy%27s_spider_monkey"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Ocellated turkey", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocellated_turkey"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Calakmul Biosphere Reserve", "icon": "lion", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sapodilla", "sp": "manilkara zapota", "xh": 0.15}, {"id": "gumbolimbo", "sp": "bursera simaruba", "xh": 0.38, "desc": "A common tree of the Yucatan forest whose small fruits are recorded in the diets of many birds, bats and primates."}, {"id": "poisonwood", "sp": "metopium brownei", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "waxmallow", "sp": "malvaviscus arboreus", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "monkey", "sp": "ateles geoffroyi", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "bat", "sp": "artibeus lituratus", "xh": 0.2, "wiki": "Artibeus lituratus", "desc": "Feeds on frui